Polyfill the global `File` class in bootstrap-fork.ts's own process, before
it loads anything else -- this embedded nodejs-mobile runtime is Node
18.20.4, which has no global `File` (a default global only since Node 20;
Node 18 exposes it only as a named export of `node:buffer`, since 18.13.0).

Confirmed via a real captured node-stdio.log, not guessed: every single
extension host connection attempt logged
"[ExtensionHostConnection] Extension Host Worker had an error" immediately
followed by "ReferenceError [Error]: File is not defined" at
node_modules/undici/lib/web/webidl/index.js:537, then "Extension Host
Worker exited with code: 1" -- vscode's bundled `undici` dependency
(pulled in transitively by the extension host's own HTTP client wiring,
e.g. `@vscode/proxy-agent`, loaded from `bootstrap-fork.js`) references the
global `File` unconditionally at module-load time. This was blocking the
extension host from starting at all, on every attempt, once the separate
EADDRINUSE bug (ipad-vscode's own NodeRuntimeController.swift fix) stopped
masking it.

Guarded (`typeof globalThis.File === 'undefined'`) so it's a no-op on any
Node build where `File` already exists as a global (Node 20+, or a real
Electron/desktop build) -- this only ever does anything on this specific
embedded, older-Node mobile runtime.

Verified the same way every other patch in this project is: the intended
edit was applied to a real copy of the pinned vscode commit's source
(08d4889f9ec4a1685d257b9b95de036c8e1ce1e5) and diffed programmatically
(rather than hand-writing hunk headers), then confirmed to apply with
`patch -p1 --fuzz=0` (zero tolerance for near-miss context) with the
resulting file byte-identical to the intended target. Not run through
`tsc` for real (no local vscode build environment in this pipeline).

Index: code-server/lib/vscode/src/bootstrap-fork.ts
===================================================================
--- code-server.orig/lib/vscode/src/bootstrap-fork.ts
+++ code-server/lib/vscode/src/bootstrap-fork.ts
@@ -222,6 +222,22 @@
 	terminateWhenParentTerminates();
 }

+// iOS: this embedded nodejs-mobile runtime is Node 18.20.4, which has
+// no global `File` (added as a default global only in Node 20 -- Node
+// 18 exposes it only as a named export of node:buffer, since 18.13.0).
+// vscode's bundled `undici` dependency (loaded transitively by the
+// extension host's own HTTP client wiring, e.g. @vscode/proxy-agent)
+// references the global `File` unconditionally at module-load time
+// (node_modules/undici/lib/web/webidl/index.js), crashing this whole
+// Worker with "ReferenceError: File is not defined" before it can even
+// finish loading -- confirmed via a real captured node-stdio.log
+// ("Extension Host Worker had an error" / "exited with code: 1" on
+// every single connection attempt), not guessed. Harmless everywhere
+// else (only applies when the global is actually missing).
+if (typeof (globalThis as any).File === 'undefined') {
+	(globalThis as any).File = (await import('node:buffer')).File;
+}
+
 // Bootstrap ESM
 await bootstrapESM();
